IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division A -- BENEFITS PAYABLE (subsection 44(1)).
--
-- Subsection 44(1) names eight benefits and says to whom each "shall be paid", "subject to this Part". This module
-- is the entitlement test of each: who qualifies, and the dates at which the conditions are tested. The payment
-- machinery (applying for the benefit, the month it starts, the amount) is in other provisions and other pieces.
--
-- What a benefit's conditions read from other provisions are inputs, named after the fact:
--   "contributor" (section 2(1): the core's `s 2(1) — a contributor`), "survivor", "disabled", "disabled contributor's child",
--   "orphan" (section 42, cp3-part2-interpretation.l4), and the minimum qualifying period (subsections 44(2) to (5),
--   cp3-minimum-qualifying-period.l4).
-- Three kinds of condition are counterfactuals: whether a benefit "would have been payable" had an application been received
-- earlier or had a division not been made (paragraphs (b), (e), (h)). They depend on the same section's other conditions
-- as they would have stood, so they are supplied as facts.
-- Ages go through section 2(2) (the core's cpp-core-age.l4), the person being treated as having reached an age at the start of the month after the birthday's month.
-- "Subject to this Part" also makes every entitlement subject to the rest of Part II (an application, the bars of sections 44.1 and
-- 44.2, the rules of payment in cp4 and cp5); this module decides the conditions of subsection 44(1) only.

§ `Part II -- Division A -- benefits payable (subsection 44(1))`

§§ `The dates of subsection 44(1)`

-- src:981 | (i) before 2019, to the survivor of a deceased contributor who has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, if the survivor
-- src:987 | (ii) after 2018, to the survivor of a deceased contributor who has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period;
@ref Act s 44(1)(d) (src:981), (src:987)
`s 44(1)(d) — the first day of 2019, the day from which "after 2018" runs` MEANS YMD 2019 1 1

§§ `44(1)(a) -- the retirement pension`

-- src:972 | 44 (1) Subject to this Part,
-- src:973 | (a) a retirement pension shall be paid to a contributor who has reached sixty years of age;
@ref Act s 44(1), (1)(a) (src:972-973)
GIVEN `the person is a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it is asked whether a retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a retirement pension is paid to a contributor who has reached 60. Reaching 60 is section 2(2)'s deemed
-- date: the first day of the month after the 60th birthday's month. Paying it needs an application (Division C, piece cp4).
-- out of range: Division C, application and payment (piece cp4): this module decides entitlement under subsection 44(1) only.
`s 44(1)(a) — a retirement pension is payable to a contributor who has reached sixty years of age` `the person is a contributor` `the person's date of birth` `the date on which it is asked whether a retirement pension is payable` MEANS
        `the person is a contributor`
    AND `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the person's date of birth` 60 `the date on which it is asked whether a retirement pension is payable`

§§ `44(1)(b) -- the disability pension`

-- src:974 | (b) a disability pension shall be paid to a contributor who has not reached sixty-five years of age, to whom no retirement pension is payable, who is disabled and who
-- src:975 | (i) has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period,
-- src:976 | (ii) is a contributor to whom a disability pension would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application for a disability pension had been received before the contributor’s application for a disability pension was actually received, or
-- src:977 | (iii) is a contributor to whom a disability pension would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made;
-- src:978 | (iv) [Repealed, 1997, c. 40, s. 69]
@ref Act s 44(1)(b) (src:974-978)
GIVEN `the person is a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it is asked whether a disability pension is payable` IS A DATE
      `a retirement pension is payable to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disability pension would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application for a disability pension had been received before the contributor's application was actually received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disability pension would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a disability pension is paid to a contributor who has not reached 65, to whom no retirement pension is payable, who is
-- disabled, and who meets one of three tests: (i) base contributions for the minimum qualifying period (subsections 44(2) to (2.2)), (ii) a disability pension would
-- have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if the application had been received earlier,
-- (iii) the same if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings had not been made. The three tests are alternatives: the text joins
-- them with a comma and "or" and not "and" (fork F12). Limb (iv) is repealed. Limbs (ii) and (iii) are counterfactuals supplied as facts.
`s 44(1)(b) — a disability pension is payable to a contributor who is disabled` `the person is a contributor` `the person's date of birth` `the date on which it is asked whether a disability pension is payable` `a retirement pension is payable to the contributor` `the contributor is disabled` `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` `a disability pension would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application for a disability pension had been received before the contributor's application was actually received` `a disability pension would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made` MEANS
        `the person is a contributor`
    AND (NOT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the person's date of birth` 65 `the date on which it is asked whether a disability pension is payable`)
    AND (NOT `a retirement pension is payable to the contributor`)
    AND `the contributor is disabled`
    AND (   `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period`
         OR `a disability pension would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application for a disability pension had been received before the contributor's application was actually received`
         OR `a disability pension would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made`)

§§ `44(1)(c) -- the death benefit`

-- src:979 | (c) a death benefit shall be paid to the estate or succession of a deceased contributor who has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period;
@ref Act s 44(1)(c) (src:979)
GIVEN `the person has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a death benefit is paid to the estate or succession of a deceased contributor who made base contributions for not less than the minimum
-- qualifying period (subsection 44(3)). The right is the estate's or succession's.
-- out of range: section 71 (piece cp5): the death benefit is paid under section 71.
`s 44(1)(c) — a death benefit is payable to the estate or succession of a deceased contributor` `the person has died` `the person was a contributor` `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` MEANS
    `the person has died` AND `the person was a contributor` AND `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period`

§§ `44(1)(d) -- the survivor's pension`

-- src:980 | (d) a survivor’s pension shall be paid
-- src:981 | (i) before 2019, to the survivor of a deceased contributor who has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, if the survivor
-- src:982 | (A) has reached 65 years of age, or
-- src:983 | (B) in the case of a survivor who has not reached 65 years of age,
-- src:984 | (I) had at the time of the death of the contributor reached 35 years of age,
-- src:985 | (II) was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children, or
-- src:986 | (III) is disabled, and
@ref Act s 44(1)(d)(i) (src:980-986)
GIVEN `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it is asked whether a survivor's pension is payable` IS A DATE
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE
      `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: before 2019, a survivor's pension is paid to the survivor of a deceased contributor with the minimum qualifying period, if the survivor has reached 65, or,
-- not having reached 65, was 35 or older at the contributor's death, or had dependent children then, or is disabled.
`s 44(1)(d)(i) — a survivor's pension is payable before 2019` `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` `the survivor's date of birth` `the date on which it is asked whether a survivor's pension is payable` `the day the contributor died` `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` `the survivor is disabled` MEANS
        `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor`
    AND `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period`
    AND (   `the survivor has reached 65`
         OR (    (NOT `the survivor has reached 65`)
             AND (   `the survivor had at the time of the death of the contributor reached 35 years of age`
                  OR `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children`
                  OR `the survivor is disabled`)))
    WHERE
        `the survivor has reached 65` MEANS
            `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the survivor's date of birth` 65 `the date on which it is asked whether a survivor's pension is payable`
        `the survivor had at the time of the death of the contributor reached 35 years of age` MEANS
            `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the survivor's date of birth` 35 `the day the contributor died`

-- src:987 | (ii) after 2018, to the survivor of a deceased contributor who has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period;
@ref Act s 44(1)(d)(ii) (src:987)
GIVEN `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: after 2018, a survivor's pension is paid to the survivor of a deceased contributor with the minimum qualifying period, whatever the survivor's age.
`s 44(1)(d)(ii) — a survivor's pension is payable after 2018` `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` MEANS
    `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` AND `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period`

-- src:980 | (d) a survivor’s pension shall be paid
-- src:981 | (i) before 2019, to the survivor of a deceased contributor who has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, if the survivor
-- src:982 | (A) has reached 65 years of age, or
-- src:983 | (B) in the case of a survivor who has not reached 65 years of age,
-- src:984 | (I) had at the time of the death of the contributor reached 35 years of age,
-- src:985 | (II) was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children, or
-- src:986 | (III) is disabled, and
-- src:987 | (ii) after 2018, to the survivor of a deceased contributor who has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period;
@ref Act s 44(1)(d) (src:980-987)
GIVEN `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it is asked whether a survivor's pension is payable` IS A DATE
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE
      `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: which of paragraphs (i) and (ii) governs turns on the date for which the pension is asked about: a date before 2019 takes (i), a date from 2019 takes (ii).
-- The text says only "before 2019" and "after 2018" and does not say what is dated; this reads it as the time at which the pension would be paid, not the date of the death
-- (NOTES.md, fork register).
`s 44(1)(d) — a survivor's pension is payable to the survivor of a deceased contributor` `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` `the survivor's date of birth` `the date on which it is asked whether a survivor's pension is payable` `the day the contributor died` `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` `the survivor is disabled` MEANS
    IF `the date on which it is asked whether a survivor's pension is payable` LESS THAN `s 44(1)(d) — the first day of 2019, the day from which "after 2018" runs`
    THEN `s 44(1)(d)(i) — a survivor's pension is payable before 2019` `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` `the survivor's date of birth` `the date on which it is asked whether a survivor's pension is payable` `the day the contributor died` `the survivor was at the time of the death of the contributor a survivor with dependent children` `the survivor is disabled`
    ELSE `s 44(1)(d)(ii) — a survivor's pension is payable after 2018` `the person is a survivor of the deceased contributor` `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period`

§§ `44(1)(e) -- the disabled contributor's child's benefit`

-- src:988 | (e) a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit shall be paid to each child of a disabled contributor who
-- src:989 | (i) has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period,
-- src:990 | (ii) is a contributor to whom a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application for a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit had been received before the application was actually received, or
-- src:991 | (iii) is a contributor to whom a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1, had not been made;
-- src:992 | (iv) [Repealed, 1997, c. 40, s. 69]
@ref Act s 44(1)(e) (src:988-992)
GIVEN `the child is a disabled contributor's child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disability pension is payable to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, under subsection (2) where a disability pension is payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, under subsection (4) where a post-retirement disability benefit is payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application had been received before the application was actually received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a disabled contributor's child's benefit is paid to each child of a disabled contributor if the contributor (i) made base contributions for the minimum
-- qualifying period, or (ii) or (iii) would have been paid a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit had the application been received earlier or a division not been made.
-- Subsection (2) supplies the minimum qualifying period if a disability pension is payable to the contributor and subsection (4) if a post-retirement disability benefit is.
-- The limbs describe the disabled contributor, not the child: the text says "child of a disabled contributor who", and a child is not the one who contributes (NOTES.md, fork register).
`s 44(1)(e) — a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable to a child of a disabled contributor` `the child is a disabled contributor's child` `a disability pension is payable to the contributor` `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the contributor` `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, under subsection (2) where a disability pension is payable` `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, under subsection (4) where a post-retirement disability benefit is payable` `a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application had been received before the application was actually received` `a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made` MEANS
        `the child is a disabled contributor's child`
    AND (   (`a disability pension is payable to the contributor` AND `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, under subsection (2) where a disability pension is payable`)
         OR (`a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the contributor` AND `the contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, under subsection (4) where a post-retirement disability benefit is payable`)
         OR `a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application had been received before the application was actually received`
         OR `a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made`)

§§ `44(1)(f) -- the orphan's benefit`

-- src:993 | (f) an orphan’s benefit shall be paid to each orphan of a deceased contributor who has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period;
@ref Act s 44(1)(f) (src:993)
GIVEN `the individual is an orphan of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: an orphan's benefit is paid to each orphan of a deceased contributor who made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period (subsection 44(3)).
`s 44(1)(f) — an orphan's benefit is payable to an orphan of a deceased contributor` `the individual is an orphan of the deceased contributor` `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` MEANS
    `the individual is an orphan of the deceased contributor` AND `the deceased contributor has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period`

§§ `44(1)(g) -- the post-retirement benefit`

-- src:994 | (g) a post-retirement benefit shall be paid to a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan who has made a contribution in respect of the post-retirement benefit; and
@ref Act s 44(1)(g) (src:994)
GIVEN `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made a contribution in respect of the post-retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a post-retirement benefit is paid to a beneficiary of a retirement pension (under this Act or a provincial plan) who has made a contribution in respect of it.
`s 44(1)(g) — a post-retirement benefit is payable to a beneficiary of a retirement pension` `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` `the person has made a contribution in respect of the post-retirement benefit` MEANS
    `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` AND `the person has made a contribution in respect of the post-retirement benefit`

§§ `44(1)(h) -- the post-retirement disability benefit`

-- src:995 | (h) a post-retirement disability benefit shall be paid to a beneficiary of a retirement pension who has not reached 65 years of age and is disabled if
-- src:996 | (i) the beneficiary has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period and that period ends after 2018,
-- src:997 | (ii) the beneficiary is a contributor to whom a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application for a post-retirement disability benefit had been received before the application was actually received, or
-- src:998 | (iii) the beneficiary is a contributor to whom a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made.
@ref Act s 44(1)(h) (src:995-998)
GIVEN `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it is asked whether a post-retirement disability benefit is payable` IS A DATE
      `the beneficiary is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the beneficiary is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(h)` IS A DATE
      `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application had been received before the application was actually received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a post-retirement disability benefit is paid to a beneficiary of a retirement pension who has not reached 65 and is disabled, if (i) the beneficiary has
-- made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period (subsection 44(4)) and that period ends after 2018, or (ii) or (iii) it would have been payable had the application been
-- received earlier or a division not been made. "That period" is read as the contributory period of subsection (5), which ends with the month of deemed disablement (NOTES.md, fork register).
`s 44(1)(h) — a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to a beneficiary of a retirement pension who is disabled` `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension` `the beneficiary's date of birth` `the date on which it is asked whether a post-retirement disability benefit is payable` `the beneficiary is disabled` `the beneficiary has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` `the month in which the beneficiary is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(h)` `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application had been received before the application was actually received` `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made` MEANS
        `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension`
    AND (NOT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the beneficiary's date of birth` 65 `the date on which it is asked whether a post-retirement disability benefit is payable`)
    AND `the beneficiary is disabled`
    AND (   (    `the beneficiary has made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period`
             AND `the month in which the beneficiary is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(h)` AT LEAST `s 44(1)(d) — the first day of 2019, the day from which "after 2018" runs`)
         OR `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if an application had been received before the application was actually received`
         OR `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable at the time the contributor is deemed to have become disabled if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings that was made under section 55 or 55.1 had not been made`)
